1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kisskh.lv =

2
00:01:06,384 --> 00:01:08,136
I saw you in Belle's posts.

3
00:01:08,972 --> 00:01:10,265
I even thought you were her boyfriend.

4
00:01:10,766 --> 00:01:11,634
Huh?

5
00:01:12,432 --> 00:01:14,350
He's just my friend!

6
00:01:14,939 --> 00:01:17,618
I still want to get to know
Belle and study her better.

7
00:01:17,778 --> 00:01:18,779
Study her?

8
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:20,356
"Study her," huh?

9
00:01:20,771 --> 00:01:22,564
What do you think
she is, a science project?

10
00:01:22,817 --> 00:01:24,861
Honestly, I'm worried...

11
00:01:25,028 --> 00:01:27,360
because we all know
that Lorenz is her trigger.

12
00:01:27,818 --> 00:01:30,238
Just always listen to this.

13
00:01:30,562 --> 00:01:33,606
No matter how complicated
Belle may be…

14
00:01:34,746 --> 00:01:38,458
I’m sure her true feelings
for you will always come through.

15
00:01:39,043 --> 00:01:41,296
But it’s still different when you
have someone to share your life with.

16
00:01:42,045 --> 00:01:43,296
Someone who also has direction.

17
00:01:43,296 --> 00:01:43,880
Belle...

18
00:01:44,547 --> 00:01:46,841
I’d like to feature you on
our magazine show.

19
00:01:47,592 --> 00:01:48,676
Okay, I'll do it.

20
00:01:49,135 --> 00:01:51,387
My name is...Ysabelle Navarro.

21
00:01:51,638 --> 00:01:53,431
I have a mental disorder.

22
00:01:54,265 --> 00:01:56,851
It's called Dissociative
Identity Disorder.

23
00:01:57,185 --> 00:01:58,227
He's just using you!

24
00:01:59,228 --> 00:02:00,772
Estong, I'm the one
who's using you.

25
00:02:01,105 --> 00:02:02,482
Actually, both of you.

26
00:02:02,750 --> 00:02:03,649
You.

27
00:03:19,642 --> 00:03:20,852
Did you think I forgot

28
00:03:20,852 --> 00:03:22,765
what you did to me on our first date?

29
00:03:27,734 --> 00:03:29,527
How you were ashamed of me?

30
00:03:29,652 --> 00:03:31,648
How you were scared of me?

31
00:03:32,498 --> 00:03:34,208
How much you were disgusted by me?

32
00:03:35,324 --> 00:03:38,244
And how you just left me on our first date?

33
00:03:39,662 --> 00:03:40,749
Well, no.

34
00:03:41,914 --> 00:03:43,124
I haven't forgotten about it.

35
00:03:43,124 --> 00:03:44,459
I'll never forget it,

36
00:03:44,459 --> 00:03:45,334
and now...

37
00:03:45,585 --> 00:03:47,420
do you think you can fool me again?

38
00:03:49,130 --> 00:03:50,465
Do you think I didn't intentionally

39
00:03:50,465 --> 00:03:52,425
reach out to you first?

40
00:03:55,845 --> 00:03:57,261
I want to make it up to her.

41
00:03:59,807 --> 00:04:01,267
Oh, there you go.

42
00:04:03,436 --> 00:04:05,229
What did you think, Lorenz?

43
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,023
That you're fooling me again?

44
00:04:07,523 --> 00:04:08,524
The past

45
00:04:08,524 --> 00:04:10,860
isn't meant to be forgotten.

46
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:13,654
It's supposed to be answered for.

47
00:04:13,738 --> 00:04:16,157
Do I really need to sign that?

48
00:04:16,616 --> 00:04:19,035
Isn’t it enough that I agreed?

49
00:04:20,495 --> 00:04:23,706
Just wait until your
show is over, Lorenz...

50
00:04:23,706 --> 00:04:25,291
You'll wish

51
00:04:25,708 --> 00:04:28,002
you had never come back to me.

52
00:04:31,964 --> 00:04:33,925
I want to prove to you...

53
00:04:34,592 --> 00:04:36,219
that I can humiliate you

54
00:04:36,761 --> 00:04:39,472
and make you hope for nothing.

55
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:43,597
And now...

56
00:04:45,019 --> 00:04:46,604
say goodbye to a good story,

57
00:04:47,438 --> 00:04:50,316
because I won't allow you to air
the footage we shot anymore.

58
00:04:51,609 --> 00:04:52,409
No.

59
00:04:52,443 --> 00:04:53,409
You can't do that.

60
00:04:54,111 --> 00:04:55,339
You agreed to do this,

61
00:04:55,530 --> 00:04:56,339
right?

62
00:04:56,364 --> 00:04:57,198
How?

63
00:04:57,824 --> 00:04:58,800
Verbally?

64
00:04:59,283 --> 00:05:00,868
You can't use that against me.

65
00:05:02,411 --> 00:05:03,394
But me...

66
00:05:05,248 --> 00:05:07,333
I have something to use against you.

67
00:05:07,667 --> 00:05:10,066
What you did was also
kind of embarrassing, right?

68
00:05:17,593 --> 00:05:20,012
Because no matter how we look at it…

69
00:05:21,347 --> 00:05:22,932
you’re still not in your right mind.

70
00:05:29,438 --> 00:05:30,773
Oh, so you’re a prick, huh?

71
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,149
You’ve been at it this whole time.

72
00:05:32,149 --> 00:05:34,193
- What, you wanna fight?
- I'm going to show everyone...

73
00:05:35,049 --> 00:05:37,448
everything you've done to me.

74
00:05:38,781 --> 00:05:41,033
Your unethical behavior

75
00:05:41,033 --> 00:05:42,994
as a media producer...

76
00:05:43,306 --> 00:05:47,644
and what you and
your Senior Story Producer

77
00:05:47,669 --> 00:05:49,045
slash girlfriend, did to me.

78
00:05:49,750 --> 00:05:51,362
Oh, right. I also knew that.

79
00:05:54,233 --> 00:05:55,698
I'll make sure...

80
00:05:56,674 --> 00:05:57,964
that both of you will get cancelled,

81
00:05:58,149 --> 00:05:59,442
and I'll make sure

82
00:05:59,467 --> 00:06:02,435
you can never work
for a media company

83
00:06:02,460 --> 00:06:03,711
ever again.

84
00:06:07,476 --> 00:06:08,355
Belle.

85
00:06:13,900 --> 00:06:15,151
Surely by now...

86
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:18,154
you've already realized
that I only used you

87
00:06:18,154 --> 00:06:20,031
so I could get back with Lorenz.

88
00:06:20,990 --> 00:06:21,741
This is on you.

89
00:06:21,741 --> 00:06:23,367
You wouldn't leave me alone,
you were so stubborn.

90
00:06:26,610 --> 00:06:27,581
So, Estong...

91
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:31,459
stay away from me.

92
00:06:32,001 --> 00:06:33,294
Leave me alone.

93
00:06:33,830 --> 00:06:34,636
Okay?

94
00:06:37,715 --> 00:06:39,425
Because you can't help me.

95
00:06:39,425 --> 00:06:40,885
You can't even help yourself,

96
00:06:40,885 --> 00:06:41,878
so how could you even help me?

97
00:06:42,803 --> 00:06:45,181
You don't need to worry about me
because I can handle myself.

98
00:06:45,181 --> 00:06:46,807
I can control all of them now.

99
00:06:47,224 --> 00:06:48,768
I don't need your help.

100
00:07:06,577 --> 00:07:07,620
What happened?

101
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:31,951
Uh...sweetheart?

102
00:07:37,650 --> 00:07:40,444
Sweetie. Drink your medicine.

103
00:07:44,156 --> 00:07:45,197
Go on.

104
00:08:00,673 --> 00:08:02,717
You asked me before what this was.

105
00:08:03,884 --> 00:08:06,012
Everything that happened while
you were gone is in here.

106
00:08:10,195 --> 00:08:11,362
What is that for?

107
00:08:11,387 --> 00:08:12,555
I don't need that.

108
00:08:13,207 --> 00:08:14,499
I don't need to know more.

109
00:08:16,564 --> 00:08:19,025
It's not really just about your
personalities, sweetheart.

110
00:08:20,026 --> 00:08:21,569
I already told you everything.

111
00:08:21,861 --> 00:08:23,946
But all of the details about

112
00:08:23,946 --> 00:08:25,990
what happened between
you and Estong are here.

113
00:08:31,954 --> 00:08:33,014
You know, sweetheart,

114
00:08:33,039 --> 00:08:34,498
Estong is a good person.

115
00:08:35,624 --> 00:08:37,918
So what you did to him was very wrong.

116
00:08:39,211 --> 00:08:42,214
It was wrong to use him just
to get revenge on Lorenz.

117
00:08:43,466 --> 00:08:44,717
He was always there for you,

118
00:08:44,925 --> 00:08:46,302
despite not fully knowing you at first.

119
00:08:47,261 --> 00:08:49,847
He protected you so many times.

120
00:08:50,181 --> 00:08:53,225
All Estong ever did was be true to you.

121
00:08:53,559 --> 00:08:54,810
He knows about your condition.

122
00:08:54,810 --> 00:08:56,020
He knows everything.

123
00:08:56,687 --> 00:08:58,022
But he never left,

124
00:08:58,230 --> 00:09:00,441
even though he had every reason to.

125
00:09:05,279 --> 00:09:07,406
That's why I empathize for Estong.

126
00:09:08,032 --> 00:09:10,785
I feel bad for him because
he's a good person.

127
00:09:11,410 --> 00:09:13,537
He just wanted you to be safe.

128
00:09:17,291 --> 00:09:19,543
But fine, if you don't
want to apologize to him...

129
00:09:20,002 --> 00:09:21,295
we won't force you.

130
00:09:22,004 --> 00:09:23,047
But I just hope...

131
00:09:23,881 --> 00:09:24,965
you'll be fair.

132
00:10:09,426 --> 00:10:10,511
Ysa is my friend.

133
00:10:11,679 --> 00:10:12,888
A close friend.

134
00:10:13,639 --> 00:10:15,474
And so are your other personalities.

135
00:10:16,058 --> 00:10:18,269
Kuya Estong, are we friends now?

136
00:10:18,269 --> 00:10:18,933
Oh, sure!

137
00:10:18,958 --> 00:10:19,667
Friends!

138
00:10:21,355 --> 00:10:23,274
You bring out the best of us.

139
00:10:24,108 --> 00:10:25,120
...getting too—

140
00:10:26,443 --> 00:10:27,545
Don't, don't, don't—

141
00:10:27,570 --> 00:10:28,279
Hey!

142
00:10:29,447 --> 00:10:30,401
...Ysa's—

143
00:10:31,782 --> 00:10:32,542
Okay—

144
00:10:34,410 --> 00:10:35,494
...for helping us—

145
00:10:36,245 --> 00:10:37,329
So I hope

146
00:10:37,538 --> 00:10:38,747
I can be friends with you too, Belle.

147
00:11:02,104 --> 00:11:04,106
Uh...can I try the...

148
00:11:04,786 --> 00:11:06,041
grilled chicken salad,

149
00:11:06,066 --> 00:11:08,527
margherita pizza, chicken barbecue pizza...

150
00:11:08,986 --> 00:11:10,184
uh, fried chicken...

151
00:11:10,362 --> 00:11:12,907
uh, two extra rice, please.

152
00:11:13,407 --> 00:11:15,284
Uh, and one...

153
00:11:16,785 --> 00:11:18,078
Ysabelle's Mocha Magic.

154
00:11:18,871 --> 00:11:22,082
Uh, make it large and zero sugar.
I'm on a calorie deficit.

155
00:11:23,125 --> 00:11:24,585
Uh, I'll also have a donut.

156
00:11:24,825 --> 00:11:25,769
Uh, okay.

157
00:11:25,794 --> 00:11:28,339
But we don't have fried chicken and rice.

158
00:11:28,339 --> 00:11:29,548
We're a café.

159
00:11:29,548 --> 00:11:30,925
Oh, okay. I'll just have
the croissant instead.

160
00:11:31,258 --> 00:11:33,177
- Oh, okay, okay.
- She said croissant, bro

161
00:11:33,177 --> 00:11:34,199
- Okay, croi—
- Estong?

162
00:11:35,804 --> 00:11:36,707
Hello.

163
00:11:39,141 --> 00:11:39,975
Bro, you got it from here, okay?

164
00:11:39,975 --> 00:11:41,435
Hey, hey, Kuya, Kuya...

165
00:11:41,810 --> 00:11:42,645
Wait, wait.

166
00:11:43,020 --> 00:11:43,979
I need to go number two.

167
00:11:43,979 --> 00:11:45,981
- You do it.
- You just went number two earlier.

168
00:11:45,981 --> 00:11:47,249
- No, no, Kuya...
- You can handle this.

169
00:11:47,274 --> 00:11:49,109
I still want to. I still want to, okay?

170
00:11:49,485 --> 00:11:51,918
This might turn into a
three or four. Come on.

171
00:11:52,488 --> 00:11:53,426
Just stay there, Kuya.

172
00:11:54,615 --> 00:11:55,653
Uh...

173
00:11:56,158 --> 00:11:57,051
Name, please.

174
00:11:57,076 --> 00:11:57,534
Chubi.

175
00:11:57,534 --> 00:11:59,119
Chubi, okay, okay. Where are you seated?

176
00:11:59,119 --> 00:12:00,246
- Oh, over there.
- Estong?

177
00:12:00,871 --> 00:12:03,249
- Uh, we'll just serve them at your table.
- Okay, thank you.

178
00:12:03,463 --> 00:12:04,762
Also, about the...

179
00:12:09,171 --> 00:12:10,130
Can we talk?

180
00:12:10,798 --> 00:12:11,757
May I take your order?

181
00:12:13,259 --> 00:12:14,593
Can we please talk?

182
00:12:17,596 --> 00:12:19,390
"Can we please talk?"

183
00:12:20,224 --> 00:12:21,809
That's not on the menu, ma'am. Sorry.

184
00:12:24,311 --> 00:12:25,854
I read the journal.

185
00:12:26,914 --> 00:12:29,291
Everything written there,
about the exhibit...

186
00:12:29,316 --> 00:12:30,901
and everything you've done for me.

187
00:12:30,901 --> 00:12:31,961
Everything...

188
00:12:31,986 --> 00:12:34,154
Everything I don't remember. I read it all.

189
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,327
Ma'am, there are customers waiting.

190
00:12:44,832 --> 00:12:46,667
It's embarrassing for me to admit this...

191
00:12:47,418 --> 00:12:49,169
but I think I owe you an apology.

192
00:12:54,133 --> 00:12:55,145
Sorry.

193
00:12:55,843 --> 00:12:57,511
I'm really sorry, Estong.

194
00:12:58,887 --> 00:13:00,723
You didn't deserve what I did to you.

195
00:13:01,890 --> 00:13:04,143
You didn't deserve
everything I said to you.

196
00:13:04,143 --> 00:13:06,403
You didn't desereve to be used like that...

197
00:13:06,937 --> 00:13:08,814
just so I could get close to Lorenz again.

198
00:13:08,839 --> 00:13:09,757
I'm sorry.

199
00:13:13,527 --> 00:13:14,559
Are you going to order?

200
00:13:15,362 --> 00:13:18,032
Because if not, maybe you should leave.

201
00:13:18,490 --> 00:13:19,617
I'm doing business here.

202
00:13:21,577 --> 00:13:22,356
Alright.

203
00:13:23,162 --> 00:13:24,455
I'll just be a customer for now.

204
00:13:25,080 --> 00:13:27,583
How many coffees do I need to order

205
00:13:27,875 --> 00:13:29,084
for you to forgive me?

206
00:13:29,793 --> 00:13:31,378
Can you afford to buy all the coffee here?

207
00:13:33,756 --> 00:13:35,841
Well, then, you can't buy my forgiveness.

208
00:13:38,927 --> 00:13:39,486
Okay?

209
00:13:39,511 --> 00:13:41,513
- One Ysabelle's Mocha—
- Sold out.

210
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:42,715
Fine, I'll have an
Americano instead.

211
00:13:42,740 --> 00:13:44,574
Okay, just move over
to the side, thank you.

212
00:13:44,808 --> 00:13:46,060
Side. Side, please.

213
00:13:46,852 --> 00:13:47,785
One Americano.

214
00:13:48,354 --> 00:13:49,418
Ma'am, your order, please!

215
00:13:49,730 --> 00:13:50,668
Estong.

216
00:13:52,608 --> 00:13:53,984
Iced Americano.

217
00:13:54,777 --> 00:13:55,567
Okay.

218
00:13:56,904 --> 00:13:57,809
Yes?

219
00:13:58,561 --> 00:13:59,457
Thank you.

220
00:14:00,324 --> 00:14:01,481
- Your order, please.
- Thank you.

221
00:14:01,575 --> 00:14:02,785
Thank you! I'll just be over there.

222
00:14:03,202 --> 00:14:04,160
Thank you.

223
00:14:06,163 --> 00:14:07,081
Thank you, Estong.

224
00:14:07,706 --> 00:14:08,723
Your order, please.

225
00:14:08,957 --> 00:14:10,250
Estong, thank you!

226
00:14:10,376 --> 00:14:11,293
Hmm, okay.

227
00:14:12,044 --> 00:14:13,253
- Here's the menu.
- You're also having an Americano?

228
00:14:17,132 --> 00:14:18,717
Two Americanos? Alright.

229
00:14:18,717 --> 00:14:19,802
Thank you.

230
00:14:21,095 --> 00:14:22,679
I'm done with number four, Kuya.

231
00:14:22,971 --> 00:14:23,680
You're done...

232
00:14:23,705 --> 00:14:26,207
Disgusting! After just being
done with number four.

233
00:14:28,764 --> 00:14:29,754
I bet

234
00:14:30,396 --> 00:14:32,189
you won't be able to resist Ate Belle.

235
00:14:34,608 --> 00:14:35,484
Are you challenging me?

236
00:14:37,569 --> 00:14:38,821
But it's true, isn't it?

237
00:14:39,154 --> 00:14:40,906
Three days max, Kuya.

238
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,699
But then again...

239
00:14:43,617 --> 00:14:44,576
maybe for you,

240
00:14:44,701 --> 00:14:45,786
it's only three minutes.

241
00:14:48,163 --> 00:14:49,123
Bro, can you just leave for a second?

242
00:14:49,123 --> 00:14:50,958
Go get the orders ready for...

243
00:14:50,958 --> 00:14:52,501
for Chubi, go ahead, go on.

244
00:14:52,501 --> 00:14:53,585
Come on, there are quite a lot of them.

245
00:14:53,585 --> 00:14:54,473
Go!

246
00:14:55,504 --> 00:14:58,048
Uh, so two Americanos.
Do you want food with that?

247
00:15:32,082 --> 00:15:32,916
I'd like to order again.

248
00:15:32,916 --> 00:15:34,626
[Humming]

249
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:36,170
I'd like to order again.

250
00:15:37,045 --> 00:15:37,880
What is it this time?

251
00:15:38,464 --> 00:15:39,923
One Ysabelle's Mocha Magic.

252
00:15:40,299 --> 00:15:41,008
It's sold out, okay?

253
00:15:41,425 --> 00:15:42,259
What do you mean, sold out?

254
00:15:42,259 --> 00:15:44,553
But you just served that
drink to two other people.

255
00:15:44,553 --> 00:15:46,680
What about her? You gave her
Ysabelle's Mocha Magic.

256
00:15:47,139 --> 00:15:47,948
That was the last one.

257
00:15:47,973 --> 00:15:49,047
How about a cappucino?

258
00:15:49,475 --> 00:15:50,453
It's also sold out.

259
00:15:51,088 --> 00:15:53,000
What kind of coffee shop
doesn't have coffee?

260
00:15:53,604 --> 00:15:54,997
You've already ordered three.

261
00:15:55,022 --> 00:15:55,914
So?

262
00:15:56,356 --> 00:15:58,742
What if Lola Iska comes
out and scolds me again?

263
00:16:04,239 --> 00:16:05,741
Mhm...

264
00:16:06,283 --> 00:16:06,867
What?

265
00:16:06,892 --> 00:16:08,560
You're still concerned.

266
00:16:09,661 --> 00:16:11,388
I'm concerned about all of my customers.

267
00:16:11,413 --> 00:16:12,831
I even suggested a salad to her.

268
00:16:14,333 --> 00:16:16,627
Estong, I'm sorry, okay?

269
00:16:16,919 --> 00:16:18,837
What do I need to do for you to forgive me?

270
00:16:18,837 --> 00:16:19,963
Do you want me to be a dishwasher?

271
00:16:19,963 --> 00:16:21,757
A barista? A server? What?

272
00:16:21,882 --> 00:16:22,966
I'll even work part-time here.

273
00:16:23,175 --> 00:16:24,149
Come on.

274
00:16:24,426 --> 00:16:26,428
So you'll forgive me. I'm sorry, okay?

275
00:16:27,054 --> 00:16:28,641
There are already a lot
of customers behind you.

276
00:16:29,272 --> 00:16:30,732
Look, there's already a line.

277
00:16:45,280 --> 00:16:46,365
- Order?
- Capuccino, sir.

278
00:16:46,532 --> 00:16:47,469
There you go.

279
00:16:48,367 --> 00:16:49,993
He's finally showing some
character development.

280
00:16:51,036 --> 00:16:51,845
Oh,

281
00:16:51,870 --> 00:16:53,372
the day's still young.

282
00:16:53,497 --> 00:16:55,082
I know your brother.

283
00:17:40,627 --> 00:17:41,433
Uh...

284
00:17:43,255 --> 00:17:44,214
Belle, dear?

285
00:17:44,339 --> 00:17:45,074
Yes?

286
00:17:45,465 --> 00:17:46,425
Sorry,

287
00:17:46,717 --> 00:17:47,968
we're closing now.

288
00:17:48,385 --> 00:17:49,245
Oh...

289
00:17:49,803 --> 00:17:51,054
I see. Okay.

290
00:17:51,597 --> 00:17:53,390
- I'll also be heading out now.
- Alright.

291
00:17:55,420 --> 00:17:57,714
Is it Estong?

292
00:17:58,387 --> 00:18:00,556
Uh...looks like he's already resting.

293
00:18:00,689 --> 00:18:01,886
He must be exhausted.

294
00:18:01,982 --> 00:18:02,956
Ah...

295
00:18:03,525 --> 00:18:04,484
It's okay.

296
00:18:04,901 --> 00:18:05,863
I'll go ahead now.

297
00:18:06,111 --> 00:18:07,144
Alright, dear.

298
00:18:08,030 --> 00:18:09,990
- Okay. Take care now.
- Thank you.

299
00:18:24,338 --> 00:18:25,272
Kuya,

300
00:18:25,297 --> 00:18:26,113
Kuya.

301
00:18:32,012 --> 00:18:32,847
Kuya,

302
00:18:33,096 --> 00:18:34,181
don't you feel bad?

303
00:18:34,181 --> 00:18:35,390
Just talk to her.

304
00:18:37,100 --> 00:18:39,144
Kuya, I think she really regrets it.

305
00:18:39,144 --> 00:18:41,355
She’s been here all day waiting for you.

306
00:18:42,856 --> 00:18:44,089
That's her choice, bro.

307
00:18:45,776 --> 00:18:48,222
I'm just worried
something might trigger her.

308
00:18:52,199 --> 00:18:53,113
So what?

309
00:18:53,367 --> 00:18:54,425
Now, it's my fault?

310
00:18:55,786 --> 00:18:57,204
It's not like that, Kuya.

311
00:19:44,543 --> 00:19:45,839
It's okay, Belle.

312
00:19:47,546 --> 00:19:48,433
What is it now?

313
00:19:50,549 --> 00:19:51,383
Nothing.

314
00:19:52,217 --> 00:19:54,386
I just want to tell you that...

315
00:19:55,178 --> 00:19:56,263
I'm proud of you.

316
00:19:57,222 --> 00:19:58,855
You apologized to Estong...

317
00:19:59,349 --> 00:20:00,934
you confronted Lorenz.

318
00:20:01,935 --> 00:20:02,917
Good job.

319
00:20:03,979 --> 00:20:05,566
I don't need your advice.

320
00:20:05,731 --> 00:20:06,940
I don't need your help.

321
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:08,525
I don't need help from all of you!

322
00:20:10,193 --> 00:20:11,738
Do you know why everything is such a mess?

323
00:20:12,821 --> 00:20:14,005
Because of you.

324
00:20:14,030 --> 00:20:16,324
Because of all of you and
everything you've done!

325
00:20:18,243 --> 00:20:21,121
I only did what I thought was right

326
00:20:21,371 --> 00:20:23,277
and what was best for all of us.

327
00:20:23,457 --> 00:20:24,516
Well, no.

328
00:20:24,541 --> 00:20:25,876
And it's none of your business.

329
00:20:25,876 --> 00:20:28,462
I don't need you, because this is my life!

330
00:20:28,826 --> 00:20:30,839
This is my life! Mine alone!

331
00:20:35,594 --> 00:20:36,730
So from now on...

332
00:20:37,345 --> 00:20:38,738
I'll handle things on my own.

333
00:20:39,264 --> 00:20:40,807
Stay out of my business.

334
00:20:40,974 --> 00:20:42,434
All of you!

335
00:20:49,232 --> 00:20:50,144
Belle.

336
00:20:58,533 --> 00:20:59,743
I can handle myself.

337
00:21:01,275 --> 00:21:02,985
I don't need anyone.

338
00:21:03,010 --> 00:21:03,720
I can handle myself.

339
00:21:03,745 --> 00:21:05,621
No one will ever hurt me again.

340
00:21:20,363 --> 00:21:22,657
- So what happened was, he saw Alora...
- Thank you!

341
00:21:22,682 --> 00:21:23,651
when she left early
and even said goodbye.

342
00:21:23,675 --> 00:21:24,643
We still got half a
kilo of orders, right?

343
00:21:24,643 --> 00:21:26,144
Ah, that's why they weren't around.

344
00:21:26,144 --> 00:21:27,354
- And guess where she went?
- Where?

345
00:21:27,354 --> 00:21:28,495
Just around Divisoria.

346
00:21:29,439 --> 00:21:33,026
She was looking for makeup that would make
her look as beautiful as you.

347
00:21:33,401 --> 00:21:34,211
Hey,

348
00:21:34,236 --> 00:21:35,081
woah...

349
00:21:35,737 --> 00:21:37,005
Wow!

350
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:39,199
Dear, do you have a photoshoot?

351
00:21:40,075 --> 00:21:41,409
Wow, sweetheart.

352
00:21:41,852 --> 00:21:43,660
You look so beautiful today!

353
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:44,995
Ate Belle,

354
00:21:45,163 --> 00:21:47,290
- how did your interview with Lorenz go?
- Oh, right!

355
00:21:47,290 --> 00:21:48,250
Is it still happening?

356
00:21:48,375 --> 00:21:49,501
When are they releasing it?

357
00:21:49,626 --> 00:21:51,586
Oh, you might become famous.

358
00:21:51,837 --> 00:21:52,956
Oh, not anymore.

359
00:21:53,213 --> 00:21:54,130
It's not happening anymore,

360
00:21:54,130 --> 00:21:56,800
and let's not talk about
people who are worthless.

361
00:21:59,003 --> 00:22:00,081
I'll get going now.

362
00:22:00,106 --> 00:22:01,608
Sweetheart, wait. Um...

363
00:22:02,059 --> 00:22:04,145
Uh, have you talked to Estong already?

364
00:22:05,926 --> 00:22:07,214
Not yet, Nang.

365
00:22:08,103 --> 00:22:10,355
I also don't want to force myself on him.

366
00:22:12,274 --> 00:22:13,253
I'll be going now.

367
00:22:13,525 --> 00:22:14,234
Wait a minute.

368
00:22:14,265 --> 00:22:16,184
Where are you going?
Want me to come with you?

369
00:22:16,945 --> 00:22:17,654
Oh, no, Nong.

370
00:22:17,654 --> 00:22:20,365
I just have something to
finish for my next commission.

371
00:22:20,866 --> 00:22:22,008
I'll be going now.

372
00:22:22,033 --> 00:22:23,618
Alright, take care, okay?

373
00:22:45,724 --> 00:22:46,785
Do you have an order?

374
00:22:51,104 --> 00:22:53,148
One large iced mocha.

375
00:22:54,930 --> 00:22:56,681
One iced mocha.

376
00:23:01,948 --> 00:23:03,035
Anything else?

377
00:23:04,576 --> 00:23:05,472
That's all.

378
00:23:06,661 --> 00:23:07,472
Okay.

379
00:23:09,539 --> 00:23:10,916
Just bring it to my table.

380
00:23:23,219 --> 00:23:25,764
Looks like you're the
one being avoided now.

381
00:23:26,932 --> 00:23:28,016
I told you, Kuya.

382
00:23:28,433 --> 00:23:29,392
Go on, sulk some more.

383
00:23:30,560 --> 00:23:31,728
And you're rubbing it in.

384
00:23:32,145 --> 00:23:32,979
What an idiot.

385
00:23:33,772 --> 00:23:34,731
But Kuya...

386
00:23:34,940 --> 00:23:36,358
she came back, okay?

387
00:23:36,733 --> 00:23:37,527
Oh, right.

388
00:23:37,859 --> 00:23:39,319
It's her routine.

389
00:23:40,875 --> 00:23:42,042
Alright, Dad. Go start cooking.

390
00:23:42,067 --> 00:23:42,792
Okay.

391
00:23:43,281 --> 00:23:45,033
Why are you bossing me around?

392
00:23:47,202 --> 00:23:48,253
May I take your order?

393
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:50,128
One of these?

394
00:23:51,039 --> 00:23:52,457
- Adel...
- Drinks? Any drinks?

395
00:23:52,582 --> 00:23:53,917
did you miss me again?

396
00:23:55,290 --> 00:23:56,875
Give the phone to Kuya Estong.

397
00:24:00,131 --> 00:24:00,941
Kuya,

398
00:24:00,966 --> 00:24:02,592
it's Adel. She wants to talk to you.

399
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:06,012
- A latte, and this one.
- Latte. Yeah, okay.

400
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:07,597
What did he say?

401
00:24:08,068 --> 00:24:09,221
Adel, what is it?

402
00:24:09,724 --> 00:24:11,434
Uh, is Ate Belle there?

403
00:24:12,769 --> 00:24:13,792
She's here.

404
00:24:13,895 --> 00:24:14,896
Why? Did something happen?

405
00:24:15,563 --> 00:24:17,440
Ninang Barbs is worried.

406
00:24:18,108 --> 00:24:20,151
She seems different today.

407
00:24:20,151 --> 00:24:22,028
She doesn't want to talk about Lorenz.

408
00:24:22,946 --> 00:24:25,156
We're all worried
she might do something.

409
00:24:40,588 --> 00:24:41,548
What's the tea?

410
00:24:41,548 --> 00:24:42,941
You know, I was just thinking...

411
00:24:42,966 --> 00:24:45,844
we should've all been
Team Estong from the start.

412
00:24:46,055 --> 00:24:50,226
Well... how were we supposed to know
Lorenz was a red flag?

413
00:24:50,448 --> 00:24:53,159
- Oh, yeah.
- I told you. We're Team Estong!

414
00:24:53,184 --> 00:24:55,270
- That's how it should've been!
- What a shame!

415
00:24:55,598 --> 00:24:56,542
You know...

416
00:24:58,023 --> 00:24:59,482
what matters is that

417
00:25:00,191 --> 00:25:02,527
Estong and Belle need to make up.

418
00:25:03,069 --> 00:25:05,363
So we all need to come together
and help them reconcile.

419
00:25:07,866 --> 00:25:10,118
They really just need to talk.

420
00:25:10,941 --> 00:25:11,720
Well, Nang...

421
00:25:11,745 --> 00:25:13,621
They're both being stubborn.

422
00:25:13,705 --> 00:25:15,832
If only we could lock them
in a room together.

423
00:25:17,208 --> 00:25:18,175
Wait. Hold on.

424
00:25:23,715 --> 00:25:24,632
Hello?

425
00:25:25,175 --> 00:25:26,634
Uh, hello?

426
00:25:27,010 --> 00:25:30,555
Um, is this Bert? Estong's father?

427
00:25:30,638 --> 00:25:32,991
Ah, yes. that's me.

428
00:25:33,016 --> 00:25:35,685
I'm Barbs. Belle's mother.

429
00:25:36,936 --> 00:25:39,748
Can we talk about the kids?

430
00:25:39,773 --> 00:25:42,358
Uh, sure. Why, is there a problem?

431
00:25:42,525 --> 00:25:44,486
Because we need to find a way

432
00:25:44,486 --> 00:25:46,821
to keep the situation from getting worse.

433
00:25:47,319 --> 00:25:49,822
Okay, I'll call you later
when I close the cafe.

434
00:25:49,908 --> 00:25:52,660
And when the whole neighborhood
isn't listening in on you.

435
00:25:56,706 --> 00:25:57,791
Here you go, thank you.

436
00:25:57,791 --> 00:25:59,125
Oh, okay. Thank you!

437
00:26:05,757 --> 00:26:07,050
Hello. Hello!

438
00:26:07,759 --> 00:26:10,220
We don't know what to do
with Belle anymore.

439
00:26:11,429 --> 00:26:12,138
Oh, I know.

440
00:26:12,806 --> 00:26:14,140
It's the same with Estong.

441
00:26:14,140 --> 00:26:15,892
I don't know what to do anymore either.

442
00:26:16,768 --> 00:26:17,644
You know,

443
00:26:18,186 --> 00:26:19,938
they're both so stubborn,

444
00:26:19,938 --> 00:26:21,356
and so are their hearts.

445
00:26:21,940 --> 00:26:22,941
Tell me about it.

446
00:26:23,358 --> 00:26:24,317
Well...

447
00:26:24,651 --> 00:26:26,861
we can't really blame them.

448
00:26:27,737 --> 00:26:30,240
You know, I'm not asking
them to be in a relationship.

449
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:31,407
All I want is for things to

450
00:26:31,825 --> 00:26:34,452
go back to how they were,
even just as friends.

451
00:26:35,870 --> 00:26:36,871
I agree.

452
00:26:36,871 --> 00:26:40,667
I'd rather they just stay friends than...

453
00:26:41,126 --> 00:26:42,418
force it, right?

454
00:26:43,466 --> 00:26:44,255
So...

455
00:26:44,587 --> 00:26:45,755
what can we do?

456
00:26:46,589 --> 00:26:47,536
Well...

457
00:26:47,715 --> 00:26:49,884
we can start with the simplest thing.

458
00:26:50,510 --> 00:26:52,762
Get them to talk things out.

459
00:26:53,388 --> 00:26:55,140
Oh, everybody's already thought of that.

460
00:26:55,390 --> 00:26:57,308
Do you think that can still
work with them?

461
00:26:59,310 --> 00:27:01,104
I don't know, but...

462
00:27:01,271 --> 00:27:03,648
it's better for us to try

463
00:27:03,815 --> 00:27:05,275
than to do nothing.

464
00:27:06,609 --> 00:27:09,070
Okay, but we need to
plan this carefully, okay?

465
00:27:09,070 --> 00:27:12,448
Because if they find
out, I'm sure they'll bail.

466
00:27:13,116 --> 00:27:14,325
Oh, you're right.

467
00:27:15,827 --> 00:27:18,121
Alright, let's plan it out, okay?

468
00:27:18,580 --> 00:27:21,958
Can you guys keep a secret
from your daughter? I know I can.

469
00:27:28,590 --> 00:27:30,233
Is he going to take much longer, Nang?

470
00:27:30,258 --> 00:27:32,343
And are you sure he really wants
to commission a painting?

471
00:27:32,886 --> 00:27:33,970
Yes, yes, dear.

472
00:27:33,970 --> 00:27:35,054
Just a little longer.

473
00:27:35,054 --> 00:27:37,557
Uh...he just came from a meeting.

474
00:27:37,891 --> 00:27:38,939
Let's just wait.

475
00:27:39,087 --> 00:27:40,103
He’ll be here soon.

476
00:27:40,602 --> 00:27:41,572
He's taking too long.

477
00:27:48,526 --> 00:27:49,376
Sweetheart.

478
00:27:51,613 --> 00:27:52,488
I'm sorry.

479
00:27:54,574 --> 00:27:55,950
What's with the drama, Nang?

480
00:27:57,827 --> 00:27:59,037
It's nothing.

481
00:27:59,621 --> 00:28:01,080
Well... I was just thinking

482
00:28:01,080 --> 00:28:03,750
that we haven't really gone out much
with your Nonong lately.

483
00:28:04,083 --> 00:28:07,611
Sometimes I feel like I spend more time
with the rice than I do with you.

484
00:28:08,796 --> 00:28:09,853
So it is drama.

485
00:28:10,632 --> 00:28:12,091
Nang, that's okay.

486
00:28:12,800 --> 00:28:15,345
And I know you're all doing
those things for me.

487
00:28:19,849 --> 00:28:20,962
But, Nanang...

488
00:28:26,272 --> 00:28:28,191
if you want, we could...

489
00:28:29,442 --> 00:28:31,319
reduce my therapy sessions.

490
00:28:32,528 --> 00:28:33,529
Why?

491
00:28:35,114 --> 00:28:36,699
Nothing. Just to...

492
00:28:37,075 --> 00:28:38,201
cut down on expenses.

493
00:28:38,292 --> 00:28:40,165
Besides, I'm doing fine now.

494
00:28:40,411 --> 00:28:41,704
Oh, no, dear.

495
00:28:41,704 --> 00:28:43,748
Don't worry about the expenses.

496
00:28:43,957 --> 00:28:46,751
As long as your Nonong
and I can, we'll help you.

497
00:28:48,670 --> 00:28:49,504
And, dear,

498
00:28:49,671 --> 00:28:51,839
there's nothing wrong with accepting help.

499
00:28:52,799 --> 00:28:55,468
You don't have to handle
everything on your own.

500
00:28:56,094 --> 00:28:59,597
You don't have to prove to yourself
that you can do it alone.

501
00:28:59,973 --> 00:29:01,111
Not just from us.

502
00:29:01,140 --> 00:29:03,559
From everyone who cares about you, too.

503
00:29:03,935 --> 00:29:04,962
Oh, stop.

504
00:29:05,770 --> 00:29:07,313
Nang, I don't want to talk about him.

505
00:29:08,439 --> 00:29:09,941
I didn't mention a name.

506
00:29:09,941 --> 00:29:12,694
But I already know what you mean.

507
00:29:13,194 --> 00:29:15,113
Sweetheart, it's not just Estong.

508
00:29:25,123 --> 00:29:26,624
Where the hell is Estong?

509
00:29:35,383 --> 00:29:36,426
Where is he?

510
00:29:44,350 --> 00:29:45,184
Estong!

511
00:29:45,264 --> 00:29:46,290
Hurry up.

512
00:29:46,686 --> 00:29:48,980
The deliveries are waiting.

513
00:29:49,105 --> 00:29:50,315
Okay, game.

514
00:29:51,316 --> 00:29:52,692
- Is this everything, Pops?
- Yeah, that's everything.

515
00:29:53,151 --> 00:29:54,444
- Wow!
- Okay, go, go ahead.

516
00:29:54,944 --> 00:29:57,405
That smells amazing.

517
00:29:57,712 --> 00:29:58,906
Perfect timing.

518
00:29:59,699 --> 00:30:01,617
- For what?
- No, uh...

519
00:30:01,617 --> 00:30:04,912
What he meant was, it's perfect timing
because you've got a lot of deliveries.

520
00:30:06,372 --> 00:30:07,582
- Come on, come on.
- Yeah, Kuya.

521
00:30:07,582 --> 00:30:11,044
It'd be be embarrassing for the
customers, right? You should smell good.

522
00:30:12,337 --> 00:30:14,922
You know what, let's do
the restaurant delivery first.

523
00:30:15,048 --> 00:30:16,257
They said it's a rush order.

524
00:30:16,382 --> 00:30:17,692
Okay, come on, come on.

525
00:30:17,717 --> 00:30:19,135
It's a restaurant. Don't
they have coffee there?

526
00:30:19,135 --> 00:30:20,511
Why does it have to be
a rush? What's the hurry?

527
00:30:20,511 --> 00:30:25,183
No, they prefer our coffee
during the staff's break.

528
00:30:25,183 --> 00:30:27,643
It's stronger, so it helps
them wake up more.

529
00:30:28,728 --> 00:30:29,687
Wait a minute, I'll just use the restroom.

530
00:30:29,687 --> 00:30:30,688
Wait, no, no, no.

531
00:30:32,231 --> 00:30:33,064
Bro,

532
00:30:33,350 --> 00:30:34,447
don't.

533
00:30:34,609 --> 00:30:35,902
They asked us to hurry, remember?

534
00:30:35,902 --> 00:30:37,278
They've been waiting for us.

535
00:30:38,071 --> 00:30:39,030
You deliver it instead, bro.

536
00:30:39,030 --> 00:30:40,490
I feel like it'll be quicker if you do it.

537
00:30:40,490 --> 00:30:42,325
- Uh, no, no.
- He'll take care of it, Pops.

538
00:30:42,325 --> 00:30:44,827
You two should just go together.

539
00:30:44,827 --> 00:30:47,455
That way, you'll get there...

540
00:30:48,122 --> 00:30:49,374
faster, right?

541
00:30:50,291 --> 00:30:52,001
What's the.. what's the difference, Pops?

542
00:30:52,994 --> 00:30:54,337
Something got in my eye.

543
00:30:57,722 --> 00:30:58,848
Hey, bro, what's happening to you?

544
00:30:58,966 --> 00:31:00,268
Nothing. I just got some
